#!/usr/bin/env python3
from pathlib import Path
import json,html,sys
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
D=json.loads((ROOT/'survey.json').read_text());rows=D['results']
def tex(x,display=True):return '<span class="math" data-display="'+str(display).lower()+'" data-tex="'+html.escape(x,quote=True)+'"></span>'
if '--skip-plot' not in sys.argv:
 import matplotlib
 matplotlib.use('Agg')
 import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
 plt.rcParams.update({'font.size':12,'axes.spines.top':False,'axes.spines.right':False,'font.family':'DejaVu Sans'})
 fig,ax=plt.subplots(figsize=(10,4.5),layout='constrained');fig.patch.set_facecolor('#f5f4ee');ax.set_facecolor('#f5f4ee')
 ns=[r['n']for r in rows];ds=[float(r['distance'])for r in rows];ps=[float(r['paperDistance'])for r in rows]
 ax.plot(ns,ds,'o-',color='#68518a',label='Best found in the selected maximal 1-AC subspace',lw=1.6)
 ax.plot(ns,ps,'s--',color='#0d7467',label='Paper family $P_N$',lw=1.4,markersize=4)
 ax.set(xlabel='Qubit number N',ylabel='Barycenter distance (sphere radius = 1)',xlim=(1.6,20.4),ylim=(-.004,.12));ax.set_xticks(ns);ax.grid(axis='y',alpha=.18);ax.legend(loc='upper left',frameon=False,fontsize=10)
 ax.annotate('N = 15: 0.106435',(15,ds[13]),xytext=(16.2,.112),arrowprops={'arrowstyle':'-','color':'#68518a'},fontsize=10,color='#68518a')
 for ext in ['png','svg']:fig.savefig(ROOT/f'barycenter-comparison.{ext}',dpi=170)
 svg=ROOT/'barycenter-comparison.svg';svg.write_text('\n'.join(line.rstrip()for line in svg.read_text().splitlines())+'\n')
 plt.close(fig)
body='''<p><a href="../../index.html#n=12&amp;t=1&amp;subspace=reflection-pairs-n12-k5-t1">← AC-subspace catalogue</a></p><p class="eyebrow">First-order anticoherence · N = 2–20</p><h1>How far can the Majorana barycenter move?</h1><p class="status">One specified maximal AC subspace per size. The zero maxima at N = 2, 3, 4 are proved. All other displayed maxima are numerical candidates; exact algebraic constructions certify the candidate states, not their optimality.</p>'''
body+='<p>We maximize the unweighted centroid distance of unit Majorana stars, counting every multiplicity:</p>'+tex(r'\mathbf b(\psi)=\frac1N\sum_{a=1}^N\mathbf n_a,\qquad d_B(\psi)=\|\mathbf b(\psi)\|,\qquad E_B=1-d_B^2.')
body+='<p>The reflection-pair and central-block constructions specify the search spaces, extending the N = 12 example. At N = 3 the space is the GHZ line. Maximal dimension does not specify a unique subspace: these are not maxima over every possible maximal AC subspace or over all first-order AC states. Every selected analytical basis is included in <a href="subspaces.json">the source-basis file</a>.</p><img class="chart" src="barycenter-comparison.svg" alt="Best candidate displacement varies non-monotonically with N, peaks at about0.106435 for N15, and exceeds the paper family for every N5 through20."><p class="caption">Lines connect computed points as a visual guide. They do not assert monotonicity, an asymptotic law or global optimality.</p><h2>Results</h2><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>N</th><th>Dimension k</th><th>Best distance</th><th>Paper distance</th><th>Largest multiplicity</th><th>State</th></tr></thead><tbody>'
viewer={}
for r in rows:
 n=r['n'];pts=[]
 for root in r['roots']:
  if root['root']is None:p=[0,0,1]
  else:
   z=complex(*map(float,root['root']));q=1+abs(z)**2;p=[2*z.real/q,-2*z.imag/q,(abs(z)**2-1)/q]
  pts.append(dict(zip(['x','y','z'],p),multiplicity=root['multiplicity']))
 viewer[str(n)]={'id':f'barycenter-n{n}','n':n,'label':f'N = {n} · barycenter distance {float(r["distance"]):.9f}','points':pts,'evidence':'Exact algebraic AC candidate. Coordinates are a numerical rendering. Maximum barycenter distance is unproved.'if n>4 else 'The zero barycenter maximum is proved for every first-order AC state at this size.'}
 body+=f'<tr><th>{n}</th><td>{r["dimension"]}</td><td>{float(r["distance"]):.12f}'+(' <span class="tag">proved</span>'if n<=4 else '')+f'</td><td>{float(r["paperDistance"]):.12f}</td><td>{max(r["multiplicityPattern"])}</td><td><button type="button" data-view-n="{n}">Sphere ↗</button> <a href="#n{n}">Coefficients ↓</a></td></tr>'
body+='</tbody></table></div><h2>What the survey suggests</h2><ul><li>Every candidate for N ≥ 5 except N = 6 has one k-fold Majorana point and N − k other points. This is an observed pattern, not a theorem about maximizers.</li><li>N = 6 is an exception: the best candidate has a double point. A triple point in a first-order AC six-qubit state forces a rotated balanced Dicke state, whose barycenter is zero.</li><li>The sequence is non-monotonic. N = 15 gives the largest displacement in this range, about 10.64% of the sphere radius.</li><li>Every candidate for N = 5–20 exceeds the displacement of the paper’s P_N family at the same size.</li></ul><h2>Comparison with the paper</h2><p>Section IV.B, Eqs. (35)–(37), of <a href="../../references/PRA90_032314(2014).pdf">Baguette, Bastin and Martin, Physical Review A 90, 032314 (2014)</a> defines the same barycentric measure and gives</p>'
body+=tex(r'|P_N\rangle=\frac{\sqrt{N-2}|D_N^{(0)}\rangle+\sqrt N|D_N^{(N-1)}\rangle}{\sqrt{2N-2}},\quad d_B(P_N)=\left|\frac{2(N-1)}{N\left[1+((N-2)/N^2)^{1/(N-1)}\right]}-1\right|.')
body+='<p>The paper’s family is an example of nonzero barycenters among first-order AC states, not a claim of maximum displacement. Its zero result for every AC state at N ≤ 4 supplies the three proved entries. Its Section III multiplicity obstruction explains the six-qubit exception.</p><h2>Analytical construction of the candidates</h2><p>Let the chosen orthonormal subspace basis be v₀,…,vₖ₋₁, with Dicke coefficients Vᵣⱼ. Define its Majorana polynomials and Wronskian:</p>'
body+=tex(r'f_j(z)=\sum_{r=0}^N(-1)^r\sqrt{\binom Nr}V_{rj}z^r,\qquad W(z)=\det\left[f_j^{(\ell)}(z)\right]_{\ell,j=0}^{k-1}.')
body+='<p>For each candidate other than N = 6, a selected simple root ζ of W defines the state through cofactors of the first k − 1 derivative rows:</p>'
body+=tex(r'A_{\ell j}=f_j^{(\ell)}(\zeta)\quad(0\le\ell\le k-2),\qquad u_j=(-1)^j\det A_{\widehat j},\qquad |\psi\rangle=\frac{\sum_j u_j|v_j\rangle}{\sqrt{\sum_j|u_j|^2}}.')
body+='<p>A simple Wronskian root guarantees a nonzero cofactor vector and exactly k-fold vanishing. The full span is first-order AC, so the constructed state is exactly AC. The <a href="root-certificates.json">15 independent rational-interval certificates</a> isolate the chosen roots and certify their simplicity. They establish an exact algebraic prescription, not global maximality. Two particularly simple root expressions are</p>'
body+=tex(r'\zeta_5=-\left(3\sqrt3+2\sqrt7\right)^{1/4},\qquad \zeta_8=\left(\frac{23+5\sqrt{22}}{\sqrt{21}}\right)^{1/5}.')
body+='<p>For N = 6, an exact radical parameter matches the numerical stationary point:</p>'+tex(r'a=\frac{1+\sqrt5}{2}+\sqrt{\frac{5+\sqrt5}{2}},\qquad a^4-2a^3-6a^2+2a+1=0.')+'<p>Use it in the explicit double-root polynomial</p>'
body+=tex(r'\begin{aligned}p_a(z)={}&(a^{10}+14a^5-1)z^3+(-6a^7+3a^2)\left(z-\frac{z^6}{3}\right)\\&+(-a^8-2a^3)(1+3z^5).\end{aligned}')
body+='<p>Divide each polynomial coefficient by (−1)ʳ√C(6,r), then normalize to obtain the Dicke coefficients. Exact division verifies the factor (z − a)² and excludes a third copy. This radical-parameter state agrees with the numerically optimized stationary value to all 80 saved decimal digits. The exact state construction does not prove optimality.</p><h2>Numerical searches and independent checks</h2>'
ss=D['searchSummary'];body+=f'<p>{ss["newRecordedStarts"]:,} new recorded search starts, plus {ss["previousN12Starts"]} previously completed N = 12 starts, compare unrestricted complex superpositions, several repeated-root manifolds and polar degeneracy strata. Finite Wronskian candidates are evaluated separately. Search failures and a small numerical residual are not optimality proofs. Discarded or interrupted exploratory batches are excluded from these counts and identified in their logs.</p>'
body+='<p>Independent 110-digit arithmetic rebuilds all 19 states from their stated subspaces, checks normalization and the one-qubit reduction, reconstructs their homogeneous polynomials from the stars, and recomputes the barycenters. All residuals are below 10⁻⁷⁸. <a href="independent-verification.json">Verification report</a> · <a href="verify_independently.py">Verifier</a> · <a href="certify_roots.py">Exact root certificate reproducer</a> · <a href="survey.json">Full results and provenance</a>.</p><h2>Explicit state data</h2><p>Decimals below are previews. High-order repeated roots are sensitive to rounding; use the full-precision downloads or the analytical kernel construction to reproduce the constellation.</p>'
for r in rows:
 n=r['n'];body+=f'<details id="n{n}" class="case"><summary>N = {n} · k = {r["dimension"]} · d = {float(r["distance"]):.12f}</summary><p>Selected subspace: <code>{html.escape(r["subspaceId"])}</code>.</p><p><button type="button" data-view-n="{n}">View Majorana sphere ↗</button> <a href="states/n{n}.json">Full-precision state and search record ↓</a></p><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Dicke index r</th><th>Real coefficient</th><th>Imaginary coefficient</th></tr></thead><tbody>'
 for j,(a,b)in enumerate(r['dickeCoefficients']):
  if max(abs(float(a)),abs(float(b)))<1e-70:continue
  body+=f'<tr><td>{j}</td><td>{float(a):+.12g}</td><td>{float(b):+.12g}</td></tr>'
 body+='</tbody></table></div></details>'
page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Majorana barycenter survey · N2–20</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../majorana-viewer.css"><script src="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.js" defer></script><script src="../../majorana-symmetry.js" defer></script><script src="../../symmetry-groups.js" defer></script><script src="../../point-groups.js" defer></script><script src="../../majorana-viewer.js" defer></script><script src="viewer-data.js" defer></script><script src="report.js" defer></script><style>body{margin:0;background:#f5f4ee;color:#263a37;font:17px/1.65 system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:1080px;margin:3rem auto;padding:0 1.5rem}h1,h2{font-family:Georgia,serif;line-height:1.2}h1{font-size:2.7rem}h2{margin-top:2.7rem}a{color:#07584d}.eyebrow{font-size:.8rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.14em}.status{padding:1rem;border-left:4px solid #976b27;background:#eee4d1}.math{display:block;overflow-x:auto;margin:1.4rem 0}.chart{width:100%;height:auto;margin-top:1rem}.caption{color:#5e6c68;font-size:.9rem}.table-scroll{overflow-x:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}td,th{padding:.6rem .75rem;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid #ccd4ce;white-space:nowrap}button{font:inherit;cursor:pointer;background:#fffdf8;border:1px solid #c3cfc6;border-radius:4px;padding:.4rem .7rem;color:#07584d}.tag{font-size:.75rem;color:#07584d}.case{padding:1rem 0;border-top:1px solid #ccd4ce}.case summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:600}code{overflow-wrap:anywhere;font-size:.85em}</style></head><body><main>'''+body+'''</main></body></html>'''
(ROOT/'index.html').write_text(page)
(ROOT/'viewer-data.js').write_text('window.BARYCENTER_STATES='+json.dumps(viewer,separators=(',',':'))+';\n')
(ROOT/'report.js').write_text("document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded',()=>{document.querySelectorAll('[data-tex]').forEach(e=>katex.render(e.dataset.tex,e,{displayMode:e.dataset.display==='true',throwOnError:true}));document.querySelectorAll('[data-view-n]').forEach(b=>b.addEventListener('click',()=>window.MajoranaViewer.open(window.BARYCENTER_STATES[b.dataset.viewN])));function reveal(){const e=document.getElementById(location.hash.slice(1));if(e?.tagName==='DETAILS')e.open=true;}window.addEventListener('hashchange',reveal);reveal();});\n")
print('Report and interactive state records built')
